config PINCTRL_TSI
	tristate "TSI chiplet IO-corner pinctrl and GPIO"
	depends on OF
	depends on TSI_CHIPLET || COMPILE_TEST
	select GENERIC_PINCONF
	select GENERIC_PINCTRL_GROUPS
	select GENERIC_PINMUX_FUNCTIONS
	select GPIOLIB
	select GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP
	select REGMAP
	help
	  Combined pinctrl and GPIO driver for the IO corners of a TSI
	  chiplet. SkyLP (IONW, IONE, IOSE, IOSW) is the only chiplet
	  described today; other chiplets add their own pad tables to the
	  same driver. Registers are reached through the TSI chiplet core
	  driver.

	  Most corner pads are multiplexed between an on-chip peripheral
	  (SPI/QSPI/OSPI, I2C/SMB, I3C, UART, I2S, PCIe PERST/MDIO, LED,
	  PWM) and GPIO. The hardware selects a function for a whole pad
	  group at once, not per pad, so a devicetree node should claim a
	  complete group.

	  This driver supersedes GPIO_TSI, which only handled the pads
	  that have no alternate function. Do not enable both for the
	  same corner.

config PINCTRL_TSI_KUNIT_TEST
	tristate "KUnit tests for the TSI pinctrl driver" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on PINCTRL_TSI && KUNIT
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Builds unit tests for the TSI pinctrl/GPIO driver: pad to
	  data-bit mapping, iomode (mux) encodings, group-wide muxing,
	  OE/IE direction encoding, write ordering and pin configuration,
	  all against a fake register model instead of hardware. Runs
	  under UML via tools/testing/kunit/kunit.py.

	  Say N unless you are developing the driver.
